# DEFECT 2558, beside it: a null read on a thread C made with no alternate
# signal stack is told without asking the library before the runtime
# (2026-11-15).
#
# Off the stack the runtime measured is not enough to make a fault another's:
# a null read on a thread a C library started for itself, in a program linking
# a Go archive it had not yet called, died at 139 once and hung twice in three
# runs when the guard asked Go's handler, and was told at 134 three of three
# once Go had been called. Every thread that runs Go code holds an alternate
# signal stack, Go's or the runtime's; a thread with none was made ready for
# no runtime's signals, and its fault is told at once. The library here ends
# the process in silence when it is handed a fault it did not make
# (`fixedbugs-2558-library.h`).

extern "fixedbugs-2558-library.h"
    function lib_ends_in_silence()
    function lib_read_on_plain_thread() -> i64

function main()
    lib_ends_in_silence()
    print("before")
    print(lib_read_on_plain_thread())
